  "term": "developmental dyslexia",
  "definition": "Developmental dyslexia is a cognitive disorder in which a person has much more difficulty understanding written or printed words than would be expected for their age, intelligence, and schooling, even though vision is intact. The reading problem is serious enough to interfere with school performance or everyday activities that depend on reading.",
